The biomni/ directory here is copied without modification from Biomni
(https://github.com/snap-stanford/Biomni, commit 400c1f366b96a35ca253e13c9b06c5076af41d65),
Copyright the Biomni authors, and is used under the Apache License, Version 2.0, whose text is
in LICENSE beside this file:

    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

license_info.md, also copied unchanged, lists the licenses of the data and software Biomni's
tools use, some of which do not permit commercial use.

Only the parts of the package its tools need are copied: biomni/tool/ (the tool functions,
their descriptions, the protocols and database schemas they read), biomni/know_how/, and the
modules they import (config.py, llm.py, utils.py, version.py, env_desc.py, env_desc_cm.py, and
__init__.py). Biomni's agent, evaluation, and retrieval code are not; virtual_lab has its own.

This directory is mounted read-only into the sandbox and put on its Python path, so code run
there imports the tools as Biomni's agent does. virtual_lab never imports it on the host: it
reads the tool descriptions and environment descriptions as data, and loads the know-how loader
from its file.
